-- title:
--   Base change of smooth chart algebras to integrally closed domains
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $R = \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ denote [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ and $x \in F_0$, with $F_0$ algebraic over the subfield generated by $x$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Write $B =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlg R F₀ {x}` for the subalgebra of elements of $F_0$ integral over $R[x]$, and assume $B$ is a smooth $R$-algebra. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $K'$ an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L(\!(q)\!)$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image $\mathrm{coeffEmb}_L(F_0)$ of $F_0$ under the map induced on Laurent series by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. Let $A$ be an integrally closed domain with fraction field $L$, equipped with an $R$-algebra structure compatible with $L$, and with an $A$-algebra structure on $K'$ compatible with $L \subseteq K'$. Let $x' \in K'$ have Laurent expansion $\mathrm{coeffEmb}_L(x)$. Then there is an isomorphism of $A$-algebras $e : A \otimes_R B \to$ `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlg A K' {x'}`, the integral closure of $A[x']$ in $K'$, such that $e(1 \otimes b)$ has Laurent expansion $\mathrm{coeffEmb}_L(b)$ for every $b \in B$.
--
--   This is the statement that formation of the chart ring of the two-chart integral model — the integral closure of $R[x]$ in a function field realised inside Laurent series — commutes with base change from $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ to an arbitrary integrally closed domain $A$ of characteristic zero, once the chart ring is smooth; no finiteness is assumed on $L/\mathbb{Q}$ and $A$ is not required to be an integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$. It is used in the study of integral models of modular curves, for the smoothness of relative dimension one of the two-chart model after base change, for primality of the ideal generated by $p$ in a chart ring, and for uniqueness of the relevant valuation subring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_algEquiv_tensorProduct_chartAlg_laurentBaseChange_of_smooth_of_isIntegrallyClosed.lean

